\title{sigfig: Numeric Vectors with Known Precision}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A semantic data type for numbers with known precision. Each element pairs a double precision value with a signed integer precision, describing the number of decimal places (or with negative precision, the powers of ten) to which the value is known. Values are displayed exactly as described by their precision, and operations on vectors of differing precision give results with the coarsest known precision (e.g. 3.2 + 4.12 is 7.3). Full values are retained in computation, so rounding error does not accumulate. The precision is stored with run length encoding using ALTREP (Alternative Representations for R Objects), allowing the same precision to be repeated many times throughout a vector with minimal memory use.
}
